==Latin==
{{wikipedia|lang=la}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|la|itc-pro|*haruspeks}}, equivalent to {{compound|la||alt1=haru-|t1=intestines|*spex}}. The first component is related to {{m|la|hīra}}; the second is from the root of {{m|la|speciō||to observe, watch}}.<ref>{{R:Nocentini|hw=aruspice}}</ref> Compare {{cog|xfa|𐌇𐌀𐌓𐌉𐌔𐌐(𐌄𐌗)}}.

{{root|la|ine-pro|*ǵʰer-|id=bowels}}
According to Nocentini<ref>{{R:Nocentini|hw=aruspice}}</ref> the first part stems from {{der|la|ine-pro|*ǵʰer-||intestine|id=bowels}}, whence also Latin {{m|la|hariolus}}, {{m|la|hernia||hernia}}, and it is cognate to Ancient Greek {{m|grc|χορδή}}, Proto-Germanic {{m|gem-pro|*garnō||intestines}} (whence German {{m|de|Garn}}) and to Lithuanian {{m|lt|žarnà||intestine}}. The component {{m|la||-spex}} can also be found in the word {{m|la|auspex}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|haruspex}}
* {{audio|la|la-cls-haruspex.wav|Audio (Classical)}}

===Noun===
{{la-noun|haruspex<3>|g=m}}

# [[diviner]] who reads from the intestines of sacrificial animals; one who practices [[haruspicy]].

